{%- comment -%}
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SYNOR · TRY · floor 3 — the tray, and the brain
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Fifty fragrances, all the same size, all the same price. Because there
  is no size to choose and no price to compare, the card can lose almost
  everything a collection card carries - the size rail, the range, the
  figure - and what is left is a small bottle you can pick up. Three to a
  row instead of two means fifteen scents on a screen instead of four,
  and that is what makes this page feel like a counter rather than a
  catalogue.

  The same tile also knows how to be a full card: the switch at the top
  right does not reload or refetch anything, it changes one class on the
  grid and the tile shows its other half. Both halves are printed by
  Liquid at page load, so the images are server-rendered either way.

  This section is also the brain for all three floors. It renders LAST,
  so it can see the box above it; the box could never see the tray. That
  is the rule this page is built on and the reason none of the behaviour
  lives up there.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}
{%- assign sid = section.id -%}

{%- assign gold  = s.gold  | default: '#C8994B' -%}
{%- assign ink   = s.ink   | default: '#1A1712' -%}
{%- assign soft  = s.soft  | default: '#6E6656' -%}
{%- assign faint = s.faint | default: '#A9A08E' -%}
{%- assign line  = s.line  | default: '#E5DFD1' -%}
{%- assign rate  = s.rate  | default: 49 -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Family palette, the same four as the collection card. The ORDER matters:
  32 of the 50 testers carry more than one family tag, and the first match
  in this list is the one the card shows and takes its colour from. woody-oud
  sat second and so won 15 times, though only 5 of these scents are actually
  oud - on the rest it is the base note, tagged alongside the family that
  really describes them. Last is where a base note belongs.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign fam_keys = 'fresh-aquatic,amber-sweet,floral-fruity,woody-oud' | split: ',' -%}

<style>
#shopify-section-{{ sid }}{background:{{ s.bg | default: '#FFFDF8' }}}

{%- comment -%} ── the row with the switch ── {%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stv{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;
  padding:{{ s.vrow_t | default: 13 }}px {{ s.pad_x | default: 12 }}px 2px}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stv .cn{font-size:{{ s.vrow_size | default: 9 }}px;letter-spacing:.2em;
  text-transform:uppercase;color:{{ faint }};font-weight:600}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stsw{margin-left:auto;display:flex;border:1px solid {{ line }};
  border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stsw button{appearance:none;border:0;background:none;
  padding:5px 11px;font:inherit;font-size:12px;color:{{ soft }};cursor:pointer;
  display:flex;align-items:center;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stsw button + button{border-left:1px solid {{ line }}}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stsw button.on{background:{{ ink }};color:{{ s.bg | default: '#FFFDF8' }}}

{%- comment -%} ── the grid, two shapes of the same tile ── {%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray{display:grid;gap:{{ s.gap | default: 8 }}px;
  padding:{{ s.grid_t | default: 10 }}px {{ s.pad_x | default: 12 }}px {{ s.grid_b | default: 16 }}px}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.v{grid-template-columns:repeat({{ s.cols_v | default: 3 }},1fr)}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:{{ s.gap_c | default: 6 }}px}

#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile{position:relative;background:{{ s.card | default: '#FFFFFF' }};
  border-radius:{{ s.radius | default: 11 }}px;overflow:hidden;cursor:pointer;
  box-shadow:0 1px 0 {{ ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.05 }},
             0 0 0 1px {{ ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.055 }};
  transition:transform .16s ease;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile:active{transform:scale(.965)}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile.on:before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;
  border-radius:{{ s.radius | default: 11 }}px;pointer-events:none;z-index:4;
  box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 {{ s.on_ring | default: 1.5 }}px {{ gold }}}

#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .im{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;
  justify-content:center;overflow:hidden;
  background:linear-gradient(180deg,{{ s.im_a | default: '#F4EEE0' }},{{ s.im_b | default: '#FBF7EE' }})}
{%- comment -%}
  ── the well is a shape, not a height ──
  A fixed pixel height was the bug: the tile's WIDTH changes with the
  number of columns, so a 104px well was a wide letterbox at two per row
  and the crop ate the top and bottom of the bottle. Driving the well by
  ratio instead means it is square at two per row, square at three, and
  square on a tablet - the bottle is always whole. The old fixed heights
  are still here behind a switch; nothing was deleted.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if s.im_mode == 'height' -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.v .im{height:{{ s.im_h_v | default: 74 }}px}
{%- else -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.v .im{height:auto;aspect-ratio:1/{{ s.im_ratio_v | default: 1 }}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  ── the photo, edge to edge ──
  This is the collection card's first locked rule and it applies here too:
  no border, no padding, nothing floating in a well. The photo fills the
  whole well - both rounded corners at the top, both square ones at the
  bottom - and is cropped rather than shrunk to fit. A tester bottle
  standing in the middle of a cream box reads as a placeholder; the same
  bottle filling the frame reads as a photograph.
{%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .im img{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;
  object-fit:{{ s.im_fit | default: 'cover' }};
  object-position:center {{ s.im_y | default: 50 }}%;
  padding:{{ s.im_pad | default: 0 }}px;
  {% if s.im_blend %}mix-blend-mode:multiply;{% endif %}}

#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .nm{
  font-family:{{ settings.sa_font_head.family | default: 'Fraunces' }},serif;
  font-weight:600;color:{{ ink }};line-height:1.22;overflow:hidden}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.v .nm{font-size:{{ s.nm_v | default: 10.5 }}px;
  padding:6px 6px 0;height:{{ s.nm_h | default: 31 }}px}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c .nm{font-size:{{ s.nm_c | default: 12.5 }}px;padding:8px 9px 0}

#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .fm{font-size:{{ s.fm_size | default: 7.5 }}px;letter-spacing:.09em;
  text-transform:uppercase;padding:2px 6px 0;font-weight:600;
  white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .add{margin:6px;height:{{ s.add_h | default: 26 }}px;
  border-radius:{{ s.add_radius | default: 7 }}px;
  border:1px solid {{ ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.16 }};background:{{ s.card | default: '#FFFFFF' }};
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  font-size:{{ s.add_size | default: 10.5 }}px;font-weight:600;color:{{ ink }}}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile.on .add{background:{{ ink }};border-color:{{ ink }};
  color:{{ s.card | default: '#FFFFFF' }}}
{%- comment -%}
  ── once it is in the tray, the button counts ──
  Tapping a tile used to toggle, so the only way to a second bottle of the
  same scent was a tap that could just as easily throw the first one away.
  The tray has always counted duplicates - the picks list holds one entry
  per bottle - so only the control was missing. Now the tile's own tap adds
  the first, and from there the stepper owns the number: − at one takes it
  back out. The count sits where ₹49 was, so the card never changes height.
{%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .add.qty{padding:0;min-width:74px;
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .add.qty button{appearance:none;border:0;background:none;
  font:inherit;font-size:15px;line-height:1;color:inherit;cursor:pointer;
  width:26px;align-self:stretch;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  -webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .add.qty button:active{opacity:.6}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttile .add.qty b{font-weight:700;font-size:11px;
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}

#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stribbon{position:absolute;top:8px;left:8px;background:{{ ink }};
  color:{{ s.card | default: '#FFFFFF' }};font-size:7.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;
  padding:3px 7px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:600;z-index:3}

{%- comment -%}
  ── ☰, the list ──
  The old second view was the same grid with bigger cards: the same three
  columns, the same cropped name, plus chips and a foot strip that said
  the price a second time. It gave a shopper no new way to look, so it is
  gone, and the markup that only served it went with it.

  A list gives them one. Fifty scents in a grid can only be read by
  picture; in a row each name gets the card's whole width, so
  "Blue Radiance / Like DOLCE & GABBANA Light Blue" arrives whole rather
  than clipped at two lines. ⊞ is for browsing by bottle, ☰ for finding by
  name — and ☰ finally means what its icon has always drawn.

  It is one grid, not a flex row, so no wrapper had to be added to the
  tile: the photo spans both rows down the left, the name and its muse
  line stack in the middle, and the button sits at the right. The two
  middle rows are equal halves that the name and the muse hug from either
  side, so the pair stays centred against a photo taller than both.
{%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.v .stribbon{display:none}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c .fm{display:none}

#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c .sttile{display:grid;align-items:center;
  grid-template-columns:{{ s.row_im | default: 66 }}px 1fr auto;grid-template-rows:1fr 1fr;
  min-height:{{ s.row_im | default: 66 }}px;column-gap:11px;padding-right:10px}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c .sttile .im{grid-column:1;grid-row:1/3;align-self:stretch;
  width:{{ s.row_im | default: 66 }}px;height:100%;aspect-ratio:auto}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c .sttile .stribbon{top:5px;left:5px;padding:2px 5px;font-size:6.5px}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c .nm{grid-column:2;grid-row:1;align-self:end;padding:0;height:auto;
  font-size:{{ s.nm_c | default: 13 }}px;
  white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
{%- comment -%}
  the buy button is the third column whether or not sa-try-detail has
  wrapped it in a split button — whichever of the two is the tile's own
  child is the one that gets placed
{%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c .sttile > .add,
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.c .sttile > .stbtn{grid-column:3;grid-row:1/3;align-self:center}
{%- unless s.ribbon_on -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stribbon{display:none}
{%- endunless -%}

{%- comment -%}
  ── the running bar ──
  It rides above the bottom menu and goes down with it, exactly like the
  checkout bar on the bag: same dock, same z range. It is the only thing
  on the page that knows the total, so it says the total and what comes
  back, and nothing else.

  It used to say that as a solid black plank across the full width, square
  at the corners. The product page's bar - the one a shopper sees far more
  often - is a floating glass pill, inset from both edges, with the figure
  on the left, a green cashback chip beside it and a dark round button at
  the end. Two bars in one shop should not be two different languages, so
  this one is now built to the product page's: same inset, same blur, same
  green, same round button.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pill_a = s.pill_op | default: 52 | divided_by: 100.0 -%}
{%- assign pill_bg = s.pill_glass | default: '#FFFFFF' | color_modify: 'alpha', pill_a -%}
{%- assign pill_ed = s.pill_edge  | default: '#FFFFFF' | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.62 -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar{position:fixed;
  left:{{ s.pill_side | default: 12 }}px;right:{{ s.pill_side | default: 12 }}px;bottom:0;
  z-index:{{ s.bar_z | default: 30 }};
  display:flex;align-items:center;border-radius:100px;padding:0;color:{{ ink }};
  background:{{ pill_bg }};
  -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur({{ s.pill_blur | default: 20 }}px) saturate(1.6);
  backdrop-filter:blur({{ s.pill_blur | default: 20 }}px) saturate(1.6);
  border:1px solid {{ pill_ed }};
  box-shadow:0 14px 30px -16px {{ ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.62 }};
  transition:transform .34s cubic-bezier(.32,.9,.36,1),
             box-shadow .3s ease,border-color .3s ease}
{%- comment -%} it drops into the menu's space, as the product page's does {%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.down{transform:translateY(var(--navh,64px))}
{%- comment -%} free delivery is a rim of gold, not a repaint {%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.done{border-color:{{ gold | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.85 }};
  box-shadow:0 14px 30px -16px {{ gold | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.75 }}}

#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .tx{flex:none;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;
  justify-content:center;gap:2px;padding:8px 11px 8px 17px}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .c{
  font-family:{{ settings.sa_font_head.family | default: 'Fraunces' }},serif;
  font-size:{{ s.bar_big | default: 19 }}px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.01em;
  white-space:nowrap}
{%- comment -%}
  This line was set in the faint ink the tray uses for asides, and at that
  weight on glass it all but disappeared - the product page sets the same
  line in the readable soft ink, so it does too.
{%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .s{font-size:{{ s.bar_small | default: 7 }}px;color:{{ soft }};
  letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap}
{%- comment -%} solid green, the way the product page prints it {%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .chip{flex:none;margin-right:9px;white-space:nowrap;line-height:1;
  display:flex;align-items:center;border-radius:100px;padding:4px 9px;
  background:{{ s.cash | default: '#0C6B52' }};color:{{ s.cash_ink | default: '#EAF6F0' }};
  font-size:7.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em}
{%- comment -%}
  The button takes the rest of the pill and is pulled a pixel out on every
  side, so it forms the pill's own right-hand cap rather than floating
  inside it. That is where the bar gets its height.
{%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .stgo{flex:1;min-width:104px;margin:-1px;border:0;cursor:pointer;
  border-radius:100px;padding:12px 14px;
  background:{{ ink }};color:{{ s.bar_ink | default: '#F6EDDA' }};
  font-family:{{ settings.sa_font_body.family | default: 'Jost' }},sans-serif;
  font-size:{{ s.bar_btn | default: 11.5 }}px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.03em;
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:6px;white-space:nowrap;
  transition:transform .18s ease}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .stgo:active{transform:scale(.985)}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .stgo .ic{width:15px;height:15px;flex:none;display:block}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .stgo .ic .fill{fill:{{ s.gold_lt | default: '#D8BC82' }};
  stroke:none;opacity:.3}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .stgo .ic .line{fill:none;stroke:{{ s.bar_ink | default: '#F6EDDA' }};
  stroke-width:1.7;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar .stgo .ic .hand{fill:none;stroke:{{ s.gold_lt | default: '#D8BC82' }};
  stroke-width:1.7;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}

{%- comment -%}
  An empty tray has no figure worth setting in the display face and nothing
  to hand back, so it speaks in the body face, drops the chip, and lets the
  words take the room the button no longer needs.
{%- endcomment -%}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.empty .tx{flex:1;padding-right:9px}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.empty .c{
  font-family:{{ settings.sa_font_body.family | default: 'Jost' }},sans-serif;
  font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.empty .s{text-transform:none;letter-spacing:.01em;
  font-size:9.5px;font-weight:400;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.empty .chip{display:none}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.empty .stgo{flex:none;min-width:0;padding:12px 20px}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.empty .stgo .ic{display:none}
#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.busy{pointer-events:none;opacity:.75}

#shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttail{height:{{ s.tail | default: 84 }}px}

@media(min-width:{{ s.desk_from | default: 750 }}px){
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stwrap{max-width:{{ s.desk_max | default: 720 }}px;margin:0 auto}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .sttray.v{grid-template-columns:repeat({{ s.cols_v_d | default: 5 }},1fr)}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar{max-width:{{ s.desk_max | default: 720 }}px;left:50%;right:auto;
    transform:translateX(-50%)}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .stbar.down{transform:translate(-50%,var(--navh,64px))}
}
</style>

<div class="stwrap">
  <div class="stv">
    <span class="cn">{{ s.vrow_text | default: 'All testers · ₹49 each' }}</span>
    {%- if s.switch_on -%}
    <span class="stsw" data-stsw>
      <button type="button" data-v="v" aria-label="Small">{{ s.icon_v | default: '⊞' }}</button>
      <button type="button" data-v="c" aria-label="List">{{ s.icon_c | default: '☰' }}</button>
    </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- paginate collection.products by 50 -%}
  <div class="sttray {{ s.view_start | default: 'v' }}" data-sttray>
    {%- for product in collection.products -%}

      {%- comment -%} find the tester variant by its size word {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign tv = blank -%}
      {%- assign word = s.match | default: '3ml' | downcase -%}
      {%- for v in product.variants -%}
        {%- assign vt = v.title | downcase | replace: ' ', '' -%}
        {%- if tv == blank and vt contains word -%}{%- assign tv = v -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if tv == blank -%}{%- assign tv = product.variants.first -%}{%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} the family, for colour {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign famk = '' -%}
      {%- for k in fam_keys -%}
        {%- assign t = 'family-' | append: k -%}
        {%- if famk == '' and product.tags contains t -%}{%- assign famk = k -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- case famk -%}
        {%- when 'fresh-aquatic' -%}{%- assign fac = s.f_aqua | default: '#3F8296' -%}{%- assign faw = s.f_aquaw | default: '#DCEBEE' -%}{%- assign famw = s.fw_aqua | default: 'Fresh Aquatic' -%}
        {%- when 'woody-oud'     -%}{%- assign fac = s.f_oud | default: '#8A5F2E' -%}{%- assign faw = s.f_oudw | default: '#EFE3D2' -%}{%- assign famw = s.fw_oud | default: 'Woody Oud' -%}
        {%- when 'floral-fruity' -%}{%- assign fac = s.f_bloom | default: '#B4707C' -%}{%- assign faw = s.f_bloomw | default: '#F6E5E7' -%}{%- assign famw = s.fw_bloom | default: 'Floral Fruity' -%}
        {%- when 'amber-sweet'   -%}{%- assign fac = s.f_amber | default: '#B8843F' -%}{%- assign faw = s.f_amberw | default: '#F7EAD2' -%}{%- assign famw = s.fw_amber | default: 'Amber Sweet' -%}
        {%- else -%}{%- assign fac = s.f_amber | default: '#B8843F' -%}{%- assign faw = s.f_amberw | default: '#F7EAD2' -%}{%- assign famw = s.fm_fallback | default: 'Tester' -%}
      {%- endcase -%}

      <article class="sttile"
               data-stp
               data-id="{{ tv.id }}"
               data-nm="{{ product.title | replace: 'SYNOR ', '' | escape }}"
               data-fc="{{ fac }}"
               data-fw="{{ faw }}"
               data-img="{% if product.featured_image %}{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 90 }}{% endif %}"
               {% unless tv.available %}data-out="1"{% endunless %}>

        <div class="im">
          <span class="stribbon">{{ s.ribbon_text | default: 'Tester' }}</span>
          {%- if product.featured_image -%}
            <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 320 }}"
                 alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | escape }}"
                 width="320" height="320" loading="lazy">
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <div class="nm">{{ product.title | replace: 'SYNOR ', '' }}</div>

        <div class="fm" style="color:{{ fac }}">{{ famw }}</div>

        <div class="add">{{ s.add_text | default: '+ ₹49' }}</div>
      </article>

    {%- else -%}
      <p style="grid-column:1/-1;padding:20px 4px;color:{{ soft }};font-size:13px">
        {{ s.empty_text | default: 'No testers here yet.' }}</p>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
  {%- endpaginate -%}
</div>

<div class="sttail"></div>

{%- comment -%}
  The button is deliberately NOT called "go". The theme hands every
  button.go to GoKwik on a capture-phase listener, which would open
  checkout before this tray had put a single tester in the cart.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="stbar empty" data-stbar>
  <div class="tx">
    <div class="c" data-stbc></div>
    <div class="s" data-stbs></div>
  </div>
  <span class="chip" data-stbk></span>
  {%- comment -%}
    The label sits in its own span because the bar rewrites it on every
    change - written straight onto the button it would take the icon with it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <button type="button" class="stgo" data-stbg>
    <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <path class="fill" d="M4.6 7.5h14.8l-1 12.1A1.9 1.9 0 0 1 16.5 21h-9a1.9 1.9 0 0 1-1.9-1.4z"/>
      <path class="line" d="M4.6 7.5h14.8l-1 12.1A1.9 1.9 0 0 1 16.5 21h-9a1.9 1.9 0 0 1-1.9-1.4z"/>
      <path class="hand" d="M8.8 7.5V6a3.2 3.2 0 0 1 6.4 0v1.5"/>
    </svg>
    <span data-stbt></span>
  </button>
</div>

<script>
(function(){
  var SEC = document.getElementById('shopify-section-{{ sid }}');
  if(!SEC || SEC.dataset.stBound) return;
  SEC.dataset.stBound = '1';

  var CFG = {
    rate      : {{ rate }},
    cur       : {{ s.currency | default: '₹' | json }},
    offWord   : {{ s.add_text | default: '+ ₹49' | json }},
    barEmpty  : {{ s.bar_empty | default: 'Your tray is empty' | json }},
    barEmptyS : {{ s.bar_empty_sub | default: 'Pick any scent below · ₹49 each' | json }},
    barEmptyB : {{ s.bar_empty_btn | default: 'Start' | json }},
    barOne    : {{ s.bar_one | default: 'tester' | json }},
    barMany   : {{ s.bar_many | default: 'testers' | json }},
    barBack   : {{ s.bar_back | json }},
    barFull   : {{ s.bar_full | default: 'Delivery is free — and every rupee comes back' | json }},
    btnOpen   : {{ s.bar_btn_open | default: 'Take the tray →' | json }},
    btnBusy   : {{ s.bar_btn_busy | default: 'Adding…' | json }},
    addUrl    : {{ routes.cart_add_url | json }},
    updUrl    : {{ routes.cart_update_url | json }},
    cartJs    : {{ routes.cart_url | append: '.js' | json }},
    wait      : {{ s.sync_wait | default: 600 }},
    navFb     : {{ s.bar_offset | default: 62 }},
    follow    : {{ s.bar_follow | default: true | json }}
  };

  var tray = SEC.querySelector('[data-sttray]');
  var bar  = SEC.querySelector('[data-stbar]');
  var go   = SEC.querySelector('[data-stbg]');
  var goT  = SEC.querySelector('[data-stbt]');
  var wk   = document.querySelector('[data-stweek]');

  {%- comment -%}
    ── the week ──
    It renders ABOVE this section, so it is found by a document-wide lookup;
    a lookup inside this section would never see it. If the merchant switches
    it off it is simply absent, and the tray and the bar carry on without it -
    neither of them ever assumes it is there.

    Note what is NOT here: no target, no capacity, no "n of N". The week has
    days, and days are a reason, not an allowance. Anything past the last day
    becomes a spare and the row keeps going, which is the whole point.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  var WK = null;
  if(wk){
    WK = {
      el     : wk,
      days   : parseInt(wk.dataset.days,10) || 7,
      labels : (wk.dataset.labels||'').split(',').map(function(x){return x.trim()}),
      rate   : parseInt(wk.dataset.rate,10) || 49,
      freeAt : parseInt(wk.dataset.free,10) || 299,
      cur    : wk.dataset.cur || '₹',
      grid   : wk.querySelector('[data-stwkdays]'),
      spares : wk.querySelector('[data-stwkspares]'),
      say    : wk.querySelector('[data-stwksay]'),
      fillEl : wk.querySelector('[data-stwkfill]'),
      pill   : wk.querySelector('[data-stwkpill]'),
      sNone  : wk.dataset.sayNone || 'Free delivery over {free}',
      sMore  : wk.dataset.sayMore || '**{left}** more and delivery is free',
      sFree  : wk.dataset.sayFree || '**Delivery is on us.**',
      pTo    : wk.dataset.pillTo || '{free} →',
      pWon   : wk.dataset.pillWon || 'Delivery free',
      spOne  : wk.dataset.spareOne || 'and {n} spare',
      spMany : wk.dataset.spareMany || 'and {n} spares'
    };
  }

  var picks = [];   // [{id,nm,img}]
  var busy  = false;

  function money(n){
    return CFG.cur + Number(n).toLocaleString('en-IN');
  }
  function bold(str){
    return String(str).replace(/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/g,'<b>$1</b>');
  }
  function fill(str,o){
    return String(str).replace(/\{(\w+)\}/g,function(m,k){
      return (o[k]===undefined ? m : o[k]);
    });
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    One bottle, drawn in the product's own family colour. The week shows a
    drawing rather than the photograph on purpose: seven lifestyle shots
    nineteen pixels wide become seven different rooms, while seven drawings
    read as one set - which is exactly what a week of scents should look like.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  function vial(c, w){
    return '<svg viewBox="0 0 26 50" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax meet"'
     + (w ? ' style="width:'+w+'px"' : '') + '>'
     + '<rect x="9.5" y="2" width="7" height="7" rx="1.4" fill="'+c+'" opacity=".9"/>'
     + '<rect x="11" y="9" width="4" height="4" fill="'+c+'" opacity=".5"/>'
     + '<path d="M6 16.5a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h8a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v27a3 3 0 0 1-3 3H9a3 3 0 0 1-3-3z" fill="'+c+'" opacity=".16"/>'
     + '<path d="M6 16.5a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h8a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v27a3 3 0 0 1-3 3H9a3 3 0 0 1-3-3z" fill="none" stroke="'+c+'" stroke-width="1.15"/>'
     + '<rect x="6" y="30" width="14" height="16.5" rx="2.6" fill="'+c+'" opacity=".32"/></svg>';
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    ── the tray and the bag are the same thing ──
    The tray used to hold its picks in the tab and hand them to the cart in
    one go at the end. That made the bag's count disagree with the bar's on
    the same screen - eleven here, six down there - and the shopper is right
    to trust the bag. So every tap now reaches the real cart, and the count
    in the menu moves with it.

    Taps are not calls, though: a tap paints straight away and the cart is
    told once the hand stops. Five quick taps are one request, not five.

    Because the cart is now where the tray lives, the tray also reads it on
    the way in - a tester added from its own product page is already in the
    tray when this page opens, which is the only way the two can keep
    agreeing. Ids the shopper has already touched in this visit are left
    alone, so a slow cart read can never undo a tap that beat it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  var cartQty = {}, touched = {}, syncT = null, syncing = false, again = false;

  function post(url, body){
    return fetch(url, { method:'POST',
      headers:{ 'Content-Type':'application/json', 'Accept':'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify(body) }).then(function(r){ return r.json() });
  }

  function paintBag(n){
    var pill = document.querySelector('[data-bag]');
    if(!pill) return;
    if(n > 0){ pill.textContent = n; pill.hidden = false } else { pill.hidden = true }
  }

  function refresh(){
    return fetch(CFG.cartJs, { headers:{ 'Accept':'application/json' } })
      .then(function(r){ return r.json() })
      .then(function(c){
        cartQty = {};
        (c.items || []).forEach(function(it){ cartQty[String(it.variant_id)] = it.quantity });
        paintBag(c.item_count);
        return c;
      });
  }

  function seed(){
    return refresh().then(function(c){
      (c.items || []).forEach(function(it){
        var id = String(it.variant_id);
        if(touched[id]) return;
        var t = tray.querySelector('[data-stp][data-id="' + id + '"]');
        if(!t) return;
        for(var i=0;i<it.quantity;i++){
          picks.push({ id:id, nm:t.dataset.nm, img:t.dataset.img, fc:t.dataset.fc });
        }
      });
      draw();
    }).catch(function(){});
  }

  function wanted(){
    var m = {};
    tray.querySelectorAll('[data-stp]').forEach(function(t){ m[t.dataset.id] = 0 });
    picks.forEach(function(p){ if(p.id in m) m[p.id] = m[p.id] + 1 });
    return m;
  }

  function queueSync(){
    clearTimeout(syncT);
    syncT = setTimeout(pushCart, CFG.wait);
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    A line already in the cart is set outright, so a minus can reach zero.
    One that is not there yet has to be added - update only moves lines it
    can already see. Anything the tray does not carry is never touched.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  function pushCart(){
    if(syncing){ again = true; return Promise.resolve() }
    var want = wanted(), ups = {}, adds = [], anyUp = false;
    Object.keys(want).forEach(function(id){
      var have = cartQty[id] || 0, n = want[id];
      if(n === have) return;
      if(have > 0){ ups[id] = n; anyUp = true }
      else if(n > 0){ adds.push({ id: parseInt(id,10), quantity: n }) }
    });
    if(!anyUp && !adds.length) return Promise.resolve();

    syncing = true;
    var chain = Promise.resolve();
    if(adds.length) chain = chain.then(function(){ return post(CFG.addUrl, { items: adds }) });
    if(anyUp)       chain = chain.then(function(){ return post(CFG.updUrl, { updates: ups }) });
    return chain.then(refresh).then(function(){
      syncing = false;
      if(again){ again = false; return pushCart() }
    }).catch(function(){ syncing = false; });
  }

  {%- comment -%} ── painting ── {%- endcomment -%}
  function drawWeek(){
    if(!WK) return;
    var n = picks.length, tot = n * WK.rate, free = tot >= WK.freeAt;

    if(WK.grid){
      var h = '';
      for(var i=0;i<WK.days;i++){
        var p = picks[i];
        h += '<div class="stwk-d'+(p?' full':'')+'"><i>'+(WK.labels[i]||'')+'</i>'
           + (p ? vial(p.fc || '#B8843F') : '<span class="dot"></span>') + '</div>';
      }
      WK.grid.innerHTML = h;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      The spares row is the proof that the week is not a wall. It appears the
      moment someone takes more than the days allow, and it is written as a
      welcome, never as an overflow warning.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    if(WK.spares){
      var extra = picks.slice(WK.days);
      if(extra.length){
        WK.spares.hidden = false;
        WK.spares.innerHTML = '<span class="lb">'
          + fill(extra.length === 1 ? WK.spOne : WK.spMany, { n: extra.length })
          + '</span>' + extra.map(function(p){ return vial(p.fc || '#B8843F') }).join('');
      } else { WK.spares.hidden = true; WK.spares.innerHTML = '' }
    }

    if(WK.fillEl) WK.fillEl.style.width = Math.min(100, tot / WK.freeAt * 100) + '%';
    if(WK.pill){
      WK.pill.className = 'stwk-pill' + (free ? ' won' : '');
      WK.pill.textContent = free ? WK.pWon
        : fill(WK.pTo, { free: WK.cur + WK.freeAt.toLocaleString('en-IN') });
    }
    if(WK.say){
      WK.say.innerHTML = bold(
        free ? WK.sFree
        : n  ? fill(WK.sMore, { left: WK.cur + (WK.freeAt - tot).toLocaleString('en-IN') })
             : fill(WK.sNone, { free: WK.cur + WK.freeAt.toLocaleString('en-IN') })
      );
    }
  }

  function drawTiles(){
    var cnt = {};
    picks.forEach(function(p){ cnt[p.id] = (cnt[p.id]||0) + 1 });
    tray.querySelectorAll('[data-stp]').forEach(function(t){
      var c = cnt[t.dataset.id] || 0;
      t.classList.toggle('on', c > 0);

      var add = t.querySelector('.add');
      if(!add) return;
      if(c > 0){
        if(!add.classList.contains('qty')){
          add.classList.add('qty');
          add.textContent = '';
          add.appendChild(stepBtn('mn', '−', 'One fewer'));
          add.appendChild(document.createElement('b'));
          add.appendChild(stepBtn('pl', '+', 'One more'));
        }
        add.querySelector('b').textContent = c;
      } else if(add.classList.contains('qty')){
        add.classList.remove('qty');
        add.textContent = CFG.offWord;
      }
    });
  }

  function stepBtn(cls, glyph, label){
    var b = document.createElement('button');
    b.type = 'button';
    b.className = cls;
    b.textContent = glyph;
    b.setAttribute('aria-label', label);
    return b;
  }

  function drawBar(){
    var tot = picks.length * CFG.rate;
    {%- comment -%}
      "Full" no longer means a box is full - there is no box. It means the
      order has crossed the shop's real free-delivery line, which is the only
      threshold on this page that actually exists.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    var full = WK ? (tot >= WK.freeAt && picks.length > 0) : false;
    bar.className = 'stbar' + (full ? ' done' : '') + (picks.length ? '' : ' empty')
                  + (busy ? ' busy' : '') + (bar.classList.contains('down') ? ' down' : '');

    var c  = SEC.querySelector('[data-stbc]'),
        sb = SEC.querySelector('[data-stbs]'),
        k  = SEC.querySelector('[data-stbk]');

    if(!picks.length){
      c.textContent  = CFG.barEmpty;
      sb.textContent = CFG.barEmptyS;
      goT.textContent = CFG.barEmptyB;
      return;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      The figure leads, the way it does on a product page: the total in the
      display face, and under it what that total is made of. What comes back
      is a chip beside it rather than a sentence under it, because it is the
      same promise every time and a sentence makes it look conditional.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    c.textContent  = money(tot);
    sb.textContent = picks.length + ' ' +
      (picks.length === 1 ? CFG.barOne : CFG.barMany) +
      (full ? ' · ' + CFG.barFull : '');
    k.textContent  = fill(CFG.barBack || '+{money} back', { money: money(tot) });
    goT.textContent = busy ? CFG.btnBusy : CFG.btnOpen;
  }

  function draw(){ drawWeek(); drawTiles(); drawBar() }

  {%- comment -%} ── taps ── {%- endcomment -%}
  SEC.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    if(!e.target || !e.target.closest) return;

    var v = e.target.closest('[data-stsw] button');
    if(v){
      tray.classList.remove('v','c');
      tray.classList.add(v.dataset.v);
      SEC.querySelectorAll('[data-stsw] button').forEach(function(b){
        b.classList.toggle('on', b === v);
      });
      try{ sessionStorage.setItem('sa_try_view', v.dataset.v) }catch(err){}
      return;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      the stepper is inside the tile, and the tile adds on tap, so it has to
      answer first and keep the tap to itself
    {%- endcomment -%}
    var st = e.target.closest('.add.qty button');
    if(st){
      var ts = st.closest('[data-stp]');
      if(!ts) return;
      if(st.classList.contains('pl')) addOne(ts); else removeOne(ts.dataset.id);
      return;
    }

    var t = e.target.closest('[data-stp]');
    if(t){
      if(t.dataset.out === '1') return;
      {%- comment -%}
        the tile's own tap puts the first bottle in; after that the stepper
        owns the count, so a stray tap on the photo can no longer undo it
      {%- endcomment -%}
      for(var i=0;i<picks.length;i++){ if(picks[i].id === t.dataset.id) return }
      addOne(t);
      return;
    }

    if(e.target.closest('[data-stbg]')){ send(); return }
  });

  function addOne(t){
    picks.push({ id:t.dataset.id, nm:t.dataset.nm, img:t.dataset.img, fc:t.dataset.fc });
    touched[t.dataset.id] = 1;
    draw(); queueSync();
  }

  function removeOne(id){
    for(var i=picks.length-1;i>=0;i--){
      if(picks[i].id === id){ picks.splice(i,1); break }
    }
    touched[id] = 1;
    draw(); queueSync();
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    ── buy now ──
    The testers are in the cart already; all that can be outstanding is a
    sync still waiting on the debounce. So the wait is cut short, that one
    push is let finish, and checkout opens on a cart that is certainly right.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  function send(){
    if(busy) return;
    if(!picks.length){
      tray.scrollIntoView({ behavior:'smooth', block:'start' });
      return;
    }
    busy = true; drawBar();
    clearTimeout(syncT);
    pushCart().then(checkout).catch(function(){ busy = false; drawBar() });
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    ── buy now means buy now ──
    The shop checks out through GoKwik, which the theme opens by calling
    onCheckoutClick on a button. Asking for it here, after the add has
    actually landed, is the whole reason the bar's button is not called
    "go": the theme's own capture-phase listener would otherwise have
    opened checkout on the cart as it stood before any of this.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  function checkout(){
    try{
      if(window.bndlr && typeof initWithBundlrDiscount === 'function'){
        initWithBundlrDiscount(go); return;
      }
      if(typeof onCheckoutClick === 'function'){ onCheckoutClick(go); return; }
    }catch(err){}
    window.location.href = '/checkout';
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    ── riding the bottom menu ──
    Same behaviour as the checkout bar on the bag: sit on top of the
    bottom menu, and go down with it when it goes down. The menu is a
    site-wide section that may render after this one, so it is polled
    for rather than assumed.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  (function dock(){
    var GAP = {{ s.pill_gap | default: 9 }};
    if(!CFG.follow){ bar.style.bottom = GAP + 'px'; return }
    var tries = 0;
    function place(nav){
      var h = nav ? (nav.offsetHeight || CFG.navFb) : 0;
      if(h === 0) h = CFG.navFb;
      bar.style.bottom = (h + GAP) + 'px';
      bar.style.setProperty('--navh', (h + GAP) + 'px');
    }
    function bind(nav){
      place(nav);
      var mo = new MutationObserver(function(){
        bar.classList.toggle('down', nav.classList.contains('down'));
        place(nav);
      });
      mo.observe(nav, { attributes:true, attributeFilter:['class','style'] });
      window.addEventListener('resize', function(){ place(nav) }, { passive:true });
    }
    function look(){
      var nav = document.querySelector('nav[data-bb]');
      if(nav){ bind(nav); return }
      if(++tries < 60) setTimeout(look, 100);
      else bar.style.bottom = (CFG.navFb + GAP) + 'px';
    }
    look();
  })();

  {%- comment -%} ── start ── {%- endcomment -%}
  try{
    var vw = sessionStorage.getItem('sa_try_view');
    if(vw === 'v' || vw === 'c'){ tray.classList.remove('v','c'); tray.classList.add(vw) }
  }catch(e){}
  SEC.querySelectorAll('[data-stsw] button').forEach(function(b){
    b.classList.toggle('on', tray.classList.contains(b.dataset.v));
  });

  seed();
  draw();
})();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Try · the tray",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "sa-try-tray",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Words" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "vrow_text", "label": "Line above the grid", "default": "All testers · ₹49 each" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "add_text", "label": "Button · not picked", "default": "+ ₹49" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ribbon_text", "label": "Corner mark", "default": "Tester" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "ribbon_on", "label": "Show the corner mark", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fm_fallback", "label": "Word when a product has no family tag", "default": "Tester" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "empty_text", "label": "When the collection is empty", "default": "No testers here yet." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The two views" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "switch_on", "label": "Show the ⊞ / ☰ switch", "default": true },
    { "type": "select", "id": "view_start", "label": "View when the page opens",
      "options": [
        { "value": "v", "label": "Small bottles (3 across)" },
        { "value": "c", "label": "Full cards (2 across)" }
      ], "default": "v" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "icon_v", "label": "Switch · small icon", "default": "⊞" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "icon_c", "label": "Switch · list icon", "default": "☰" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "cols_v", "min": 2, "max": 5, "step": 1, "label": "Small view · per row", "default": 3 },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Which variant is the tester" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "match", "label": "Size word to look for", "default": "3ml",
      "info": "The first variant whose name contains this is used. If none matches, the first variant is used." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "rate", "min": 9, "max": 199, "step": 2, "unit": "₹", "label": "Price of one tester", "default": 49,
      "info": "Used for the running total. Keep it the same as in the box." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "currency", "label": "Currency mark", "default": "₹" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The bar at the bottom" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_empty", "label": "Empty · line 1", "default": "Your tray is empty" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_empty_sub", "label": "Empty · line 2", "default": "Pick any scent below · ₹49 each" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_empty_btn", "label": "Empty · button", "default": "Start" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_one", "label": "Word for one", "default": "tester" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_many", "label": "Word for many", "default": "testers" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_back", "label": "Cashback chip", "default": "+{money} back" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_full", "label": "Added to line 2 once delivery is free", "default": "free delivery" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_btn_open", "label": "Bar button", "default": "Buy now" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bar_btn_busy", "label": "Button while adding", "default": "Adding…" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "bar_follow", "label": "Ride the bottom menu", "default": true,
      "info": "Off = the bar sits at the very bottom of the screen." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "bar_offset", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "label": "Bottom menu height (fallback)", "default": 62 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "sync_wait", "min": 200, "max": 1500, "step": 50, "unit": "ms", "label": "Wait before telling the cart", "default": 600,
      "info": "A tap paints at once; the cart is told once the hand stops, so quick taps cost one request." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "bar_z", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "label": "Bar layer", "default": 30,
      "info": "Keep between 21 and 39 so it stays above the page and below the menu." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "bar_big", "min": 13, "max": 26, "step": 0.5, "unit": "px", "label": "Bar figure size", "default": 19 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "bar_small", "min": 6, "max": 12, "step": 0.5, "unit": "px", "label": "Bar small line size", "default": 7 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "bar_btn", "min": 9, "max": 16, "step": 0.5, "unit": "px", "label": "Bar button size", "default": 11.5 }
    ,{ "type": "header", "content": "The bar's glass" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pill_side", "min": 0, "max": 28, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "label": "Inset from the edges", "default": 12 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pill_gap", "min": 0, "max": 24, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "label": "Gap above the menu", "default": 9 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pill_blur", "min": 0, "max": 40, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "label": "Blur behind the glass", "default": 20 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pill_op", "min": 20, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "%", "label": "Glass opacity", "default": 52 },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Colour" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Page paper", "default": "#FFFDF8" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "card", "label": "Tile paper", "default": "#FFFFFF" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "im_a", "label": "Photo well · top", "default": "#F4EEE0" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "im_b", "label": "Photo well · bottom", "default": "#FBF7EE" },
